{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Then Moses stood.</b> So is the custom in every camp, that one stands in one place, just as it is a year to make booths and for there to be gates to the camp, for there is no need for any hand outside the camp." "<b>Whoever is for YHWH.</b> Let him come to me, or draw near, or come, or assemble." "<b>The sons of Levi.</b> For they are of his family."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:52.580076078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}